 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "Which Phuket Michelin restaurant should I book ahead?",
   "a": "Pru, the island's only one-star and a Green Star holder, is a set-menu fine-dining room starting around 7,200 baht, so reserve well ahead. Most of the Bib Gourmand spots are walk-in, though popular ones sell out, so go early."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is the cheapest Bib Gourmand in Phuket?",
   "a": "Roti Chaofa starts at just 10–30 baht, and Khao Tom Dibuk and Pathongko Mae Pranee also land in the low tens. They make excellent, wallet-friendly breakfasts and snacks for Michelin-listed food."
